mode script

// Issue #326 reachability regression fixture.
//
// A program that mentions no compiler AST type and no reflection must not
// carry the compiler's own data model into its output. `println` alone used
// to drag in StructDef -> Declaration -> Expr -> NodeType and, through
// NodeType's payloads, every type in src/core/ast.til: a generic container
// lowers to `macro(T: Type) returns StructDef`, and the scavenger rooted
// that comptime signature as if it were a runtime dependency. `println`
// takes `..Dynamic`, so every program paid for it -- 4,149 lines of C for
// this file, against 681 once macro signatures stopped being roots and 276
// once a reached type stopped rooting all five lifecycle methods.
//
// The suite asserts on the generated C (minimal_reach_no_ast_model and
// minimal_reach_no_dead_lifecycle in src/tests.til) and runs the program
// interpreted and compiled (the `both` entry), so the fixture proves both
// that the dead declarations are gone and that what survives links and runs.

// An unread top-level value with an effect-free initializer is swept, not
// kept as a blanket root (minimal_reach_no_unread_global). KEPT_GLOBAL
// proves the sweep is reachability, not a blanket rule: it is read below,
// so it must survive.
UNREAD_GLOBAL := 41
KEPT_GLOBAL := 42

println("minimal", KEPT_GLOBAL.to_str())
